WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.115
Choosing models and configurations with the eval.

2
00:00:03.395 --> 00:00:07.043
Once the eval exists, model selection stops being a debate.

3
00:00:07.323 --> 00:00:16.773
Run the same scenarios, trials, and graders for each candidate configuration: a model choice, an effort setting, a tool design, a guard variant.

4
00:00:17.053 --> 00:00:20.104
Plot success rate against cost per successful task.

5
00:00:20.384 --> 00:00:25.525
Configurations that are beaten on both axes by another (dominated) can be dropped.

6
00:00:25.805 --> 00:00:38.115
The rest form a frontier, and choosing among them is a product decision you can now state plainly: “the larger model gets one more weekly report right in twenty, at about twice the cost per report.

7
00:00:38.395 --> 00:00:38.692
”.

8
00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.874
Two patterns are worth testing for this kind of agent.

9
00:00:42.154 --> 00:00:59.306
Routing by step: a small, inexpensive model (for example claude-haiku-5-5 ) turns each issue into a fixed-schema record, and a more capable model ( claude-opus-5-5 or claude-sonnet-5-5 ) writes the report from the records.

10
00:00:59.586 --> 00:01:05.132
This is also lesson 11’s map-reduce pattern, so it can improve safety and cost at once.

11
00:01:05.412 --> 00:01:13.583
Effort: on current Claude models, a lower effort setting reduces tokens and tool calls; measure whether quality holds before you choose.

12
00:01:13.863 --> 00:01:20.498
Check the pricing page on the day you run the comparison, and record the prices in your results, because they change.

13
00:01:20.778 --> 00:01:26.580
Public agent benchmarks (Studio 3, lesson 11) can help you pick which models to try.

14
00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:30.935
They can’t tell you which wins on your scenarios, with your tools and your guard.

15
00:01:31.215 --> 00:01:46.532
AgentDojo is a useful exception for one property: it measures utility and injection robustness together, so it is a reasonable shortlist signal for agents that read untrusted content, before your own injection suite gives the real answer.
